# Copy to backend/.env and fill in. backend/.env is gitignored - NEVER commit, zip or paste the real key.
# Nothing here is required: without a key every feature uses its deterministic path.
#
# --- LLM: Bosch Model Farm (BMF) ---
# (An existing Model Farm .env with FARM_API_KEY / FARM_DEPLOYMENT_NAME / FARM_BASE_URL / FARM_API_VERSION also works.)
# Then check it on your network:   cd backend && python -m app.llm_client check
LLM_API_KEY=
# A deployment name from the BMF "Model Endpoint Reference" (Azure OpenAI API table). Developer-subscription
# deployments (marked with a star there) that suit this job:
#   askbosch-prod-farm-openai-gpt-4o-mini-2024-07-18     (plain chat parameters - recommended)
#   gpt-5-nano-2025-08-07                                  (reasoning model - handled, but slower)
# Avoid Gemini 2.5 Flash-Lite: the reference lists its retirement for 2026-10-20.
LLM_DEPLOYMENT=
#
# Defaults shown; change only if `check` says the path / version / auth is wrong:
# LLM_BASE_URL=https://aoai-farm.bosch-temp.com/api
# LLM_API_VERSION=2025-04-01-preview
# LLM_CHAT_PATH=/openai/deployments/{deployment}/chat/completions
# Auth: default "both" = custom key header + Authorization: Bearer (confirmed working on the real gateway).
# Other values: all (adds api-key, as the Azure SDK sends), azure (custom+api-key), key_header, bearer.
# LLM_AUTH_MODE=both
# A version known to work on this gateway (used by existing Model Farm client code), if the default is refused:
# LLM_API_VERSION=2023-12-01-preview
# LLM_KEY_HEADER=genaiplatform-farm-subscription-key
# Your subscription id (for the token dashboard): the reference page used for this build does not name the
# header it goes in - take the header name from the BMF "Getting Started"/"Charging" page and put it here:
# LLM_EXTRA_HEADERS={"<header-name-from-the-docs>": "<your-subscription-id>"}
# LLM_SEND_MODEL=1
# LLM_TIMEOUT=30
# Behind a corporate proxy: set HTTPS_PROXY in the environment. If TLS verification fails:
# LLM_CA_BUNDLE=C:\path\to\corporate-ca.pem
# If this machine cannot resolve aoai-farm.bosch-temp.com itself (Test-NetConnection says name resolution failed)
# but your browser can open it, a proxy is resolving names for the browser. Use the same proxy here:
# LLM_PROXY=http://<proxy-host>:<port>
# On Windows where the browser gets its proxy from a PAC script (diagnose shows 'AutoConfigURL'), let Windows
# work it out for you instead:
# LLM_PROXY=auto
# If the proxy answers HTTP 407 (it wants your Windows login) the tool switches to PowerShell by itself on
# Windows. To force it, or to turn it off:  LLM_TRANSPORT=powershell  |  LLM_TRANSPORT=python
# LLM_TRANSPORT=auto
#
# Which features may call the LLM. Default is only the flagged-pin explainer (signal names, mux options and
# net traces - no workbook rows). chat / value_decoder / node_extractor send workbook rows or DTS text:
# enable them only if your data rules allow it.
# LLM_FEATURES=usb_advice,usb_propose     (usb_propose = the AI-proposed DTS: sends this run's USB nodes + your facts)
